# .publish-denylist.example — template for scripts/publish-guard.sh
#
# publish-guard already blocks, with NO configuration:
#   - ANY real public IPv4 literal (RFC5737 / RFC1918 / loopback / link-local /
#     CGNAT / multicast are allowed) — so you do NOT need to list a host IP here.
#   - ANY real public IPv6 literal (2001:db8::/32 doc / fc00::/7 unique-local /
#     fe80::/10 link-local / ::1 loopback / ff00::/8 multicast are allowed) —
#     the validator host is dual-stack, so this covers the IPv6 address too.
#   - the operator handle and the validator SSH key name, matched by embedded
#     sha256 (the raw words are never stored in the tracked script).
#
# Use a local .publish-denylist ONLY to add EXTRA exact substrings the two
# built-in layers do not cover (e.g. an internal hostname alias, a second SSH
# key name, a colo/rack identifier). One exact substring per line; lines
# beginning with # are comments; blank lines ignored.
#
# Setup (the real file is gitignored — it may contain sensitive strings):
#   cp .publish-denylist.example .publish-denylist
#   # then add real forbidden substrings, one per line, to .publish-denylist
#
# This .example file is TRACKED and PUBLIC — it MUST NOT contain any real
# secret. The placeholders below are illustrative only; replace them.
#
# internal-host-alias.example
# secondary-ssh-key-name
# rack-or-colo-identifier
